<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Stadtholderless Period</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1650–1672</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Stadtholderless Period was the era from 1650 to 1672 when the leading provinces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> left the office of stadtholder vacant after the death of William II of Orange. Government was led by the regents of Holland under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-pensionary">Grand Pensionary</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johan-de-witt">Johan de Witt</a>, who favoured trade and kept the house of Orange from power. It ended in the Disaster Year of 1672, when the French invasion brought William III to power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-stadtholderless-period.jpg" alt="First Stadtholderless Period" width="320" height="412" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: After Jan de Baen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grand_Pensionary_Johan_de_Witt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
